# Git Workflow

- Keep pull requests small and focused; target roughly 400 changed lines or less when practical.
- Split unrelated work into separate commits or PRs.
- Write commit messages in English, imperative mood, and focus on why the change exists.
- Use branch prefixes that describe intent: `feature/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `docs/`, or `test/`.
- Never commit secrets, credentials, `.env` files, `.npmrc`, or files under `tools/env/*`.
- Before committing, review staged changes and ensure unrelated user changes are not included.
